CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ braced-init arg reads reference member once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ by-value braced-init arg reads reference member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ reference member observes referand mutation: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG: must fail: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.ref]/1 + [expr.unary.op]/1: a reference denotes the object it binds
to, and the built-in unary * applied to a reference operand yields that object.
A reference lvalue -- notably an access to a reference data member `this->ref`
-- is materialised by add_implicit_dereference as an implicit dereference_exprt
whose operand keeps the reference type.  That node is fully type-checked when it
is built, but the same argument sub-tree can reach typecheck_expr a second time:
a braced-init-list call argument such as `combine({ref, base})` is type-checked
once by the operand walk and again while the call's arguments are converted to
the parameter's class type (constructing a temporary).  The generic operand walk
(typecheck_expr_operands, run before typecheck_expr_main) then re-type-checked
the operand `this->ref`, whose member access re-applied its own implicit
dereference; the outer * ended up wrapping the already-dereferenced value,
corrupting `*this->ref` into the ill-formed `*(*this->ref)` and rejecting the
program with "operand of unary * '*this->ref' is not a pointer".  In modern STL
this surfaced as spurious "instantiating std::__enable_if_t with <FALSE, ...>"
cascades (the enable_if frames were correctly SFINAE-suppressed; the fatal error
was the downstream reference-member double-dereference) -- e.g. compiling
src/util/irep_serialization.cpp's
  ireps_container.ireps_on_write.insert({h, ireps_container.ireps_on_write.size()})
where ireps_container is a reference data member.  Fixed in
cpp_typecheckt::typecheck_expr by recognising an already-elaborated implicit
dereference of a reference operand (id==dereference, C_implicit, result type
set, operand of reference type) and leaving it untouched before its operands are
walked.  assertion.4 provides non-vacuity.
